# Rules Routing Table

Host-maintained lookup that maps a task to the rule files it requires. Agent
Smith reads this table, matches the current task against it, and passes the
listed file paths to `agent_smith_select_rules`. The server then walks the
agent through those files one at a time.

## How Agent Smith uses this table

- File paths are **relative to `lore/rules_md/`** (e.g. `api/handlers.md`).
- **Multi-select:** pick EVERY row that plausibly matches the task and combine
  their file lists. Duplicates are removed automatically by the server. When a
  task spans concerns (e.g. an API change that also touches the database),
  select all relevant rows.
- **Do NOT list `core/` files.** Everything under `lore/rules_md/core/` is
  always read automatically, on every task. Keep core rows out of this table.
- **When unsure or nothing matches:** call `agent_smith_select_rules` with an
  empty list. The server then mandates ALL rule files. Reading too much is
  always safer than missing a rule.
- If any listed path no longer resolves (a rule was renamed/moved and this
  table is stale), the server falls back to reading ALL rule files.

## Maintaining this table (for humans)

Add one row per task category your repository cares about. Each row lists the
task-specific rule files under `lore/rules_md/` that a task of that kind must
follow. Replace the example rows below with your project's real rule files.

| Task | Rule files to read (relative to lore/rules_md/) |
|------|--------------------------------------------------|
| Add or modify a REST API endpoint | `api/handlers.md`, `api/validation.md` |
| Add or modify a database migration or schema | `db/migrations.md`, `db/models.md` |
| Frontend / UI component work | `ui/components.md`, `ui/state.md` |
| Write or change automated tests | `testing/conventions.md` |
| CI / pipeline / build configuration | `ci/pipelines.md` |
| Anything touching authentication or secrets handling | `security/auth.md` |
| General refactor, cleanup, or task that fits no row above | _(leave empty — all rules apply)_ |
